The original is already a single null check and a load, so there is little to gain. This version adds a branch-prediction hint that the null case is rare. Behavior is unchanged for every input.

```cpp
FIT_UINT16 Mesg::GetNum() const
{
#if defined(__GNUC__) || defined(__clang__)
    if (__builtin_expect(profile == FIT_NULL, 0))
        return FIT_MESG_NUM_INVALID;
#else
    if (profile == FIT_NULL)
        return FIT_MESG_NUM_INVALID;
#endif

    return profile->num;
}
```